# Late-applied 2D (K-grouped) scales vs. systolic k-chain length.
#
# On Xe3p/CRI, f8:f8 with block scales on BOTH src and wei takes the "late
# quantization" path: scales are applied while repacking C, once every
# gcd(aqGroupK, bqGroupK) k-elements. The systolic k-chain advances
# ksys * kChain k-elements at a time (32 * 2 = 64 for f8). If the chain spans
# more k-elements than the scale period, C is flushed less often than the
# scales change and whole scale groups are silently dropped, producing a
# wrong result with no error reported.
#
# The cases below sweep the scale group size against the k-chain span and
# include single-sided and no-scale controls, so a regression shows up as a
# specific subset failing rather than everything at once.
#
# K is always >= 2 * group so that multiple scale groups exist along K, and
# group < K so the scales are not folded away as a single per-tensor value.

--reset
--dt=f8_e4m3:f8_e4m3:bf16
--wtag=acb
--grouped=0:4:8+8+8+8

# group == ksys (32): k-chain must be trimmed, else every other group is lost
--attr-scales=src:3:e8m0:1x32+wei:7:e8m0:32x1
32x128:4x128x64
32x256:4x256x64
32x512:4x512x64

# group == 2 * ksys (64): a k-chain of 2 is legal here and must be preserved
--attr-scales=src:3:e8m0:1x64+wei:7:e8m0:64x1
32x128:4x128x64
32x256:4x256x64
32x512:4x512x64

# group == 4 * ksys (128)
--attr-scales=src:3:e8m0:1x128+wei:7:e8m0:128x1
32x256:4x256x64
32x512:4x512x64

# asymmetric groups: repack period is gcd(aqGroupK, bqGroupK)
--attr-scales=src:3:e8m0:1x32+wei:7:e8m0:64x1
32x256:4x256x64
--attr-scales=src:3:e8m0:1x64+wei:7:e8m0:32x1
32x256:4x256x64

# single-sided controls: these take a different path and must stay correct
--attr-scales=src:3:e8m0:1x32
32x256:4x256x64
--attr-scales=wei:7:e8m0:32x1
32x256:4x256x64

# no-scale control: k-chaining itself must remain unaffected
--attr-scales=
32x256:4x256x64

# non-e8m0 scale types bypass BDPAS and force the late-quant path
--reset
--dt=f8_e4m3:f8_e4m3:bf16
--wtag=acb
--grouped=0:4:8+8+8+8
--attr-scales=src:3:f16:1x32+wei:7:f16:32x1,src:3:f16:1x64+wei:7:f16:64x1
32x256:4x256x64

# f4_e2m1: ksys is 64, so the group/chain relationship differs from f8
--reset
--dt=f4_e2m1:f4_e2m1:bf16
--wtag=acb
--grouped=0:4:8+8+8+8
--attr-scales=src:3:e8m0:1x32+wei:7:e8m0:32x1
32x256:4x256x64
32x512:4x512x64
